  <result type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened framework conditions and institutional capacity to promote urban water management and climate adaptation and resilience in cities with a focus on water related challenges.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="276134" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Key policy, regulatory or procedural obstacles for enhancing urban climate resilience through water efficiency, water resource planning, wastewater treatment and storm water management have been addressed.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="identification of obstacle"></target>
     <actual value="Process plan for developing a Water Security Strategy for the City of Tshwane has been decided and the initials steps towards an as is analysis are made. The Climate Adaptation and Wastewater Management Plan was approved by the assembly in Tema and ready for implementation.
10 SOPs for operation of Temba wastewater treatment plant are developed and being implemented. And a pilot wastewater treatment plant has been selected and O&amp;M plan has been commented in India.
Concept for improved leak management in selected cities in Rajasthan has been initiated based on data collection and analysis.
A concept for GIS platform has not been developed in Rajasthan, but a working group with members for local, state and national level has been formed."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-12-31"></period-end>
